modsPerl - MODS Command Scripting Engine
Release Notes
Updated: 2011 Oct 31 [rwp/osu]

This file gives the release notes for the MODS runtime scripting engine,
which is currently implemented in Perl.  See the 00README file for 
a general description of modsPerl.

See: www.astronomy.ohio-state.edu/MODS/ObsTools/modsTools/ for a 
     description of the MODS observing scripting system.

---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Release Notes:

2011 Oct: Version 1.1 - Minor changes after the Sept 2011 science runs,
          added WFSWait command to execMODS for imaging scripts
          changed print color to Cyan for visibility.

          Added true SIGINT (Ctrl+C) handling to execMODS and acqMODS, 
          including a more sophisticated post-abort cleanup routine, 
          and a normal end-of-script cleanup capability.

          Added the modsMask command to operate either the MODS1 or
          MODS2 mask system for performing slit mask exchanges.

          Minor change to ISIS.pm to say what command timed out.
    
    Version Summary:
        acqMODS  0.7.1
        execMODS 1.8.3
        execISIS 0.1.0
        modsCmd  0.5.8 
        isisCmd  1.0.3 
        modsMask 0.1.3  <-- new this release


2011 May: Version 1.0 - first non-beta release
   execMODS - added abort/retry/ignore on errors
              added -u/--unattended to allow unattended operation and
                suppress abort/retry/ignore (e.g., for morning unattended
                calibrations).
              added nimgs=1 implicit on obsmode/calmode/setupmode
              Ready for non-beta release.
   listMODS - added handling for implicit nimgs above
   acqMODS  - extended abort/retry to include ignore like execMODS,
               but no unattended mode (not indicated).
               ready for non-beta release
   modsCmd  - added Getopt::Long for command-line option handling, and
               now use -t to allow timeouts. Has interesting consequences
               if command arguments include negative numbers.  May regret...
   execISIS - New tool.  Used to run "scripts" of ISIS commands.  Will keep
               this away from observers, but useful for support scripts.
               Will beta test during May run, but likely early release.


2011 Apr: Version 0.7.0
   execMODS - changed myID, numerous bug fixes as we used it heavily.
              this should be the last beta version (hooray!)
   acqMODS - Beta version, many changes.  Exercised extensively during this
             run. Does implicit IMCS, resets nimgs, and numerous
             bug fixes.  Added abort/retry prompt on errors.
   ISIS.pm - DONE: et al. tests are now case insensitive!  Funny how
             long that went unnoticed (all automatic systems use all upper
             but sending done: by hand revealed the problem).


2011 Mar: Version 0.6.0
   execMODS - implicit IMCSLOCK following INSTCONFIG
              implemented full block-level re-entrancy, including
                run-from and run-only block options.
              added color to error messages
   acqMODS - added ACQROI to allow changing CCD ROI for acquisition
             added color to error messages
   listMODS - support for the IMCSLOCK implicit command in execMODS
              so we don't screw up command numbers for reentrancy.
              gratuitous color printout support


2011 Feb: Version 0.5.0
   acqMODS - Beta version tested, working out detailed procedures
   execMODS - added PAUSE command.  Added Getopt::Long for smart 
              command-line option handling.  Added and tested script 
              re-entrancy and limited -e Exec: block re-entrancy.
   listMOD - now prints block labels w/o numbers, better for execMOD
             re-entrancy
   modsCmd - replacment for doMODS (but keeping as an alias)


2011 Jan: Version 0.4.0
   Telescope disabled, so extensive testing and extension of execMODS and
   listMODS. Minor work on ISIS.pm to make timeout handling more robust.  
   Sketched out acqMODS, but until we get some time on-sky, it is mostly 
    notional at this point.  
   isisCmd written to provide a direct comm tool for low-level ISIS commands.


2010 Dec: Version 0.3.0
   Extensive development of execMODS during a run of extremely bad weather
   (we never opened).  Added PRINT command, and added stripFirst routine
   to take care of internal commands.  Extensive exercising.  First 
   version of listMODS.


2010 Nov: Version 0.2.0 
   Developments for MODS1 at LBT as it nears the end of AGw commissioning.
   Changes to doMODS, first version of execMODS from OSU on the mountain.
   The latter is first true scripting engine in alpha release.


2010 June: Version 0.1.0
   Beta version at LBT: updates to the ISIS.pm module and field versions 
   of various lab scripts from OSU.  First instance of the doMODS script
   send single data-taking system commands to the MODS control panel backdoor.



